From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:05:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] protocol: serialize pipeline binaries

VP_ANDROID_17_requirements lists VK_KHR_pipeline_binary. Unlike the other
extensions the profile still wanted, it is not struct-only: it introduces the
VkPipelineBinaryKHR object and five commands, so it needs command identifiers
as well as a list entry. They take 371 to 375, after the range the local
device-address topic already claimed.

The five commands are also grouped with the pipeline module rather than left
to the catch-all. Only vkDestroyPipelineBinaryKHR matched a rule, through the
DestroyPipeline prefix, which would have put VkPipelineBinaryKeyKHR's codecs
in one header and four of the five commands that use them in another that is
included first.

The extension table grows from 204 entries to 205.

A pipeline key and a pipeline binary are derived from the pipeline creation
structure the caller chains onto VkPipelineCreateInfoKHR, and that structure
is a pipeline create info in its own right, so vk.xml gives it no
structextends="VkPipelineCreateInfoKHR". The generated chain codec therefore
knew of nothing to carry and always encoded a null pNext: the renderer handed
its driver a create info that described nothing, which the driver read without
checking. The registry fixup names the three pipeline create infos the
extension can be asked about as the chain's children. A chain is encoded flat,
each node's own pNext through the chain codec of the structure the chain
belongs to, so the structures that extend a pipeline create info join the same
chain; without them a dynamic-rendering or pipeline-binary chain would be
dropped along with the create info's own extensions.

The roundtrip test carries a graphics pipeline create info with its own
dynamic-rendering chain through the encoder and the renderer's temporary
decoder, and checks every truncation of that stream is refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
